/-
P3 (line jboot, gen 5): **the un-narrowed decode lemmas of U2's cone on irqfix's `MachPlatT`, the IRQ ack by
`IrqAckU`** (irqfix's IrqFixC did the same for the narrowed `Fl4ProofsI` copies in U32's cone).

U2 (`serializable_fl4_localU2`) reaches P3 through `kernel_entry_reachU17V`'s lineage, whose decode lemmas are
KEntry39/40's `jDecMRL_of`, `jDecMRL2_ofT`, `jDecMRLK_ofU` (not ArchIrqNarrowGen's copies). For the transport of
U2's cone (P2/WitU34Gen) they are replaced by:
* `jDecMRL_ofQ0` (KEntry39 verbatim, generated by `scratch/jboot5/genC.py`): `hM : MachPlatT`, `hDL : JDecMRL2Q`
  (= `JDecMRL2 ∧ IrqAckU`); the IRQ handler's ack (`mask_irq irq false`) by `hDL.2` (irqfix's `IrqAckU`) where
  the original used `MachPlat.mask`; the IO port / IRQ handler / IRQ control helpers by their transported copies
  (`Fl4ProofsQ.P3.XCapP.mr`, `.mrG`, `.mF_mr` from irqfix's run B, `decode_invocation_irq_controlXSM` from
  JBoot5GenB).
* `jDecMRL2_ofTQ0`, `jDecMRLK_ofUQ0`: JBoot5GenB's copies carrying `IrqAckU` along (`JDecMRLKQ` ↦ `JDecMRL2Q`,
  `JDecMRLKQ` ↦ `JDecMRLKQ`).
`IrqAckU` stays inside the decode premise (`JDecMRLKQ`), which only the tops' syscall clauses take; U2's proof
never instantiates those clauses, so it never has to supply it.

No premise; no sorry. New module; no existing statement changed.
-/
